  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 20,
    "summary": "Wine is a mocker, and strong drink is raging—Turn to the Lord, and He will save you.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Wine is a mocker, strong drink is raging: and whosoever is deceived thereby is not wise.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "TG Drunkenness; Temperance; Word of Wisdom."
          },
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Mocking."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 7
          },
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 33
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The fear of a king is as the roaring of a lion: whoso provoketh him to anger sinneth against his own soul.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "Prov. 19:12."
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 76,
            "text": "Mosiah 17:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 21
          },
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 53
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 92
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "It is an honour for a man to cease from strife: but every fool will be meddling.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "TG Strife."
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "Ether 12:26."
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "IE fomenting trouble."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The sluggard will not plow by reason of the cold; therefore shall he beg in harvest, and have nothing.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "TG Apathy; Idleness."
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "HEB winter; i.e., after the autumn harvest."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 59
          },
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 93
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Counsel in the heart of man is like deep water; but a man of understanding will draw it out.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "D&C 78:2."
          },
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "D&C 11:26."
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "Prov. 18:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Most men will proclaim every one his own goodness: but a faithful man who can find?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The just man walketh in his integrity: his children are blessed after him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "TG Walking with God."
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "TG Integrity."
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG Family."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 12
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 55
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A king that sitteth in the throne of judgment scattereth away all evil with his eyes.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "Prov. 25:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Who can say, I have made my heart clean, I am pure from my sin?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "Rom. 3:23."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "D&C 49:8; 109:34."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Divers weights, and divers measures, both of them are alike abomination to the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 19
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Even a child is known by his doings, whether his work be pure, and whether it be right.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "Matt. 7:16 (16–20)."
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 53,
            "text": "TG Work, Value of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 56
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 80
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The hearing ear, and the seeing eye, the Lord hath made even both of them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Love not sleep, lest thou come to poverty; open thine eyes, and thou shalt be satisfied with bread.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "TG Laziness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 63
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "It is naught, it is naught, saith the buyer: but when he is gone his way, then he boasteth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 90,
            "text": "TG Boast."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          },
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 19
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "There is gold, and a multitude of rubies: but the lips of knowledge are a precious jewel.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "Job 28:18 (12–19)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 71
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Take his garment that is surety for a stranger: and take a pledge of him for a strange woman.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "Prov. 27:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Bread of deceit is sweet to a man; but afterwards his mouth shall be filled with gravel.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "IE Food gained by fraudulent means."
          },
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "TG Deceit."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 18
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Every purpose is established by counsel: and with good advice make war.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "D&C 69:4."
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 61,
            "text": "Luke 14:31."
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "Prov. 24:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that goeth about as a talebearer revealeth secrets: therefore meddle not with him that flattereth with his lips.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG Gossip."
          },
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 100,
            "text": "TG Flatter."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 22
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whoso curseth his father or his mother, his lamp shall be put out in obscure darkness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "Prov. 19:26; 1 Ne. 2:11; Mosiah 13:20."
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "Job 18:5."
          },
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 85,
            "text": "Alma 26:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "An inheritance may be gotten hastily at the beginning; but the end thereof shall not be blessed.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 21
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Say not thou, I will recompense evil; but wait on the Lord, and he shall save thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "TG Forbear; Retribution."
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "Ps. 25:5; 27:14; Isa. 40:31; 2 Ne. 6:13 (7, 13); D&C 98:2."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 41
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Divers weights are an abomination unto the Lord; and a false balance is not good.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 68,
            "text": "OR deceptive scales (i.e., made to deceive)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 18
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 71
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Man’s goings are of the Lord; how can a man then understand his own way?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "Jer. 10:23."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 16
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "It is a snare to the man who devoureth that which is holy, and after vows to make inquiry.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          },
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 28
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 52
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A wise king scattereth the wicked, and bringeth the wheel over them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "TG Kings, Earthly."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The spirit of man is the candle of the Lord, searching all the inward parts of the belly.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 20
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Mercy and truth preserve the king: and his throne is upholden by mercy.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The glory of young men is their strength: and the beauty of old men is the gray head.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "TG Glory."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "TG Beauty."
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "TG Old Age."
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "Lev. 19:32; Prov. 16:31."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 25
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The blueness of a wound cleanseth away evil: so do stripes the inward parts of the belly.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "IE flogging, strokes, blows."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
